.DS_Store

# Per-developer check overrides. Only `timeout_seconds` is honoured from here;
# every other key is ignored with a warning, because a setting that changes what
# a check examines — or whether it blocks — has to be a committed, team-visible
# decision, not one developer's local choice.
.claude/productizer/checks.local.yaml
.claude/productizer/checks.local.yml

# Eval run artifacts. Regenerated per run, and they carry the absolute paths of
# whoever ran them -- the same leak that shipped in v4.2.0. The numbers belong in
# the backlog and the docs; the raw run does not belong in git.
evals/results/

# The private half of the hygiene deny list: an employer and several private
# project names. It is read at runtime and never committed - a deny list in a
# public repo is a map of exactly which names its author is hiding, which
# defeats the point of hiding them. The shipped check carries generic rules
# only (credentials, personal paths, private keys) and loads this if present.
# The canonical copy lives outside every repository, under the home directory.
.claude/productizer/hygiene-local.txt
.claude/productizer/publish-checklist.md

# The check runner writes this. It is NOT committed, and that is deliberate: it
# records one run on one machine, so a committed copy describes somebody's local
# working state rather than a property of the tree you cloned. The version that
# used to sit here named files that do not exist in a fresh clone, and a fresh
# clone's dashboard presented that as "the last check run" for the tree in front
# of you - a recorded measurement nobody took, with no merge involved.
#
# Nothing is lost by its absence. Every reader was checked and already degrades
# honestly: build-view.sh renders the unmeasured marker, stage-status.sh says
# "not run", signals.sh reports ABSENT, and CI never reads it at all - the
# workflow writes its own copy to a temp directory.
.claude/productizer/checks-result.json
